| C1 | Inconsistency | CRITICAL | data-model.md:L184 (§5.2) vs data-model.md:L149, L366 (§11); contracts C-4 L58; tasks.md:L37, L39 | The agents decoder rule says every element of `stop.argsBeforePid` must match `/^\/[A-Z]$/`. The pinned value is `['/T', '/F', '/PID']`, and `/PID` fails that regex. If the rule is built as written, every `Win32LaunchSpec` is rejected and the launch ends as `launch-failed`, so US-1 cannot work at all. The rule is also looser than BE-010 expects: BE-010 wants "anything other than `/T /F`" rejected, but `/X` passes the regex. | Replace the regex in §5.2 with an exact match on the pinned array `['/T','/F','/PID']`. Align the BE-010 negative cases (`/IM`, `-T`, `/t x`, `/X`, missing `/PID`). |
| F1 | Inconsistency | HIGH | spec.md:L179 (FR-011) vs AD-058 Decision 3 table (L35-41), data-model.md §9.4 (L318-325), glossary.md:L1054 | FR-011 says the process tree MUST NOT remain on app exit, explicitly including "abnormal end of the session thread". The glossary defines the session thread as the Worker. AD-058 and §9.4 do not guarantee "Worker abnormal termination (`terminate()` / OOM)" for claude.exe or its descendants, and do not guarantee descendants after a supervisor abnormal exit. FR-011's second sentence lets the ADR state which endings are not guaranteed, so the requirement contradicts itself. | Reword FR-011: the guarantee covers forced stop, close, normal app exit, renderer reload and a JS exception in the session thread. Worker or supervisor abnormal termination is best-effort, per AD-058 Decision 3. |
| F2 | Inconsistency | HIGH | spec.md:L184 (FR-014) vs plan.md:L54-55, L80; tasks.md BE-010 (L36), BE-030 (L68) | FR-014 says the Windows launch and stop *implementation* must stay inside `src/main/infra/runtime/`. The plan puts `stopTree()`, the Win32 decoder (`.exe` checks, the `/X` args rule), `windowsHide: true` and the Win32 `composeClaudeSpawn` row in `src/agents/`. Principle II (no `process.platform` outside runtime/) is not broken, but the literal wording of FR-014 is, and platform-boundary-reviewer will likely flag it. | Narrow FR-014 to "platform branching, plus building the Windows launch and stop values (paths, args, env)". Alternatively, record in AD-058 that agents run the data-driven `stop` / `cwd` / `windowsHide` without knowing the platform. |
